(1245028, 154798, 34868, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by shot:</b></div><hr/><i> Wrong challenge ? I''m really disappointed from the dpchallenge members. Of course he''s the best friend of the photographer. It''s a beautiful picture and shows the best friend. I really don''t understand why all this children and animal pictures are higher rated than this here. It''s not difficult to make a photo of two cued kids or two ducks and name them "best friends". This here shows the real friendship between two people. Otherwise the photographer wouldn''t have had devoted the whole picture to " Jok "  <br/>It''s a pity that people are not thinking a little bit further and try to see what''s behind a picture. Anyway, Sofap for me it''s the best picture of the challenge together with "Beautiful Anneu". </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>shot<br/> <br/>All I can say is thank you. I received 38 comments and most said that it did not fit the challenge. This was my first, and I thought we were to be creative. I did get other comments that got the point, very few. <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by shot: Wrong challenge ? I''m really disappointed from the dpchallenge members. Of course he''s the best friend of the photographer. It''s a beautiful picture and shows the best friend. I really don''t understand why all this children and animal pictures are higher rated than this here. It''s not difficult to make a photo of two cued kids or two ducks and name them "best friends". This here shows the real friendship between two people. Otherwise the photographer wouldn''t have had devoted the whole picture to " Jok "  It''s a pity that people are not thinking a little bit further and try to see what''s behind a picture. Anyway, Sofap for me it''s the best picture of the challenge together with "Beautiful Anneu".   shot All I can say is thank you. I received 38 comments and most said that it did not fit the challenge. This was my first, and I thought we were to be creative. I did get other comments that got the point, very few. ', '2005-03-23 09:00:42.000000', NULL, 0),
